# Call-site ledger of autojump at 06e082c91805cb022900819b2e0881eeae780d58.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# autojump.md shows how this ledger applies them. The analysed source is
# bin/autojump_data.py, bin/autojump_match.py and bin/autojump_utils.py
# (root bin). The main script bin/autojump and the vendored
# autojump_argparse.py are outside: they are client code, and what the main
# script passes is a client value, as what the tests pass. Module-level
# functions are public (rule C); the 11 lexical lambdas retain their actual
# captured values and callback argument flow. The package defines no class.
# Public arguments are client objects (opaque, B5) unless a docstring fixes
# a concrete type (B4; a
# parameter's name is not documentation), or the package itself passes the
# value. Python 2.6+ and 3.3+
# are supported, so the Python 2 branches run; their builtin callees have
# the Python 3 name of the type (README, "Judgements").

